INT. HARBOR FISH AUCTION HALL - 4 A.M.

Concrete. Wet. Gulls screaming under the rafters. Rows of tuna on ice, long as men.

CARMELO "CHAR" IGLESIAS, 40s, rubber boots, gutting knife, sweeps the floor like a man hiding something.

A bell clangs. Crowd noise.

At the end of the aisle, DOM VASQUEZ, 50s, tailored raincoat, stands over a crate with a briefcase at his feet. Beside him, a skinny kid, TWITCH, 19, in a hoodie, hand twitching in his pocket.

CHAR
Dom.

DOM
Char. Product?

CHAR
Under the bluefin.

TWITCH
Under the what?

CHAR
Fish, kid.

Char tips a tuna on its side. Underneath: a taped brick.

DOM
Count it.

TWITCH
I'll count it.

CHAR
Let him.

TWITCH
All here.

DOM
Good. Case.

Dom nudges the briefcase forward with his toe. Char kneels. Lifts it. Opens. Dollars, banded. He snaps it shut.

Behind them a SHADOW moves. Char sees it first.

CHAR (CONT'D)
Don't turn around.

DOM
Who?

CHAR
Just don't.

Footsteps on wet concrete. Slow. Then DETECTIVE MARGUERITE LAWSON, 40s, windbreaker, badge on a lanyard, a gun in her right hand, steps out between two ice tubs. Her eyes flick across the three of them: Char, the brick, the briefcase, the kid.

LAWSON
Police. Hands.

TWITCH
Oh, God.

DOM
Detective.

CHAR
Marguerite.

LAWSON
Char, you son of a bitch.

TWITCH
I didn't do anything.

DOM
Kid, shut up.

Twitch bolts. Slips on fish scales. Falls. The brick skids across the floor and splits, white powder bursting like flour in the lamp light. Dom lunges for the briefcase. Char drops it. Lawson fires once into the rafters.

BANG. Gulls explode upward.

Everyone freezes.

LAWSON (CONT'D)
Nobody moves.

A long beat. Dom raises his hands. Twitch lies still. Char folds his arms.

CHAR
(softly)
You're early, Marguerite.

LAWSON
(softly)
You're late, Carmelo.

She holsters her weapon. Takes the briefcase. Walks to the edge of the dock, tosses it into the black harbor. It sinks without a ripple.

DOM
What the hell?

LAWSON
Go home, Dom. Take the kid.

She turns her back on them.
